---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="About — Haidar System" description="What Haidar System is, why it exists, and how it approaches practical digital systems.">
  <section class="wrap page" aria-labelledby="about-title">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1 class="page-title" id="about-title">A personal system for turning real problems into useful action.</h1>
    <div class="about-grid">
      <h2>What this is</h2>
      <div class="about-copy">
        <p>Haidar System is a personal operating brand for building practical digital systems around real problems and opportunities. It connects thinking, experiments, capabilities, and project proof under one clear operating structure.</p>
        <p>It is broader than a developer portfolio and more restrained than an agency promise. Software, AI, automation, research, and emerging technology are tools used when they fit the problem.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="about-grid">
      <h2>How projects are approached</h2>
      <div class="about-copy">
        <p><strong>Real problem → clear system → practical action → measurable proof.</strong></p>
        <p>Work begins by understanding the problem and available demand evidence. The next step is the smallest reliable system that can create useful action or learning. Outcomes and uncertainty are then documented honestly.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="about-grid">
      <h2>What is being learned</h2>
      <div class="about-copy">
        <p>The current direction is demand intelligence: discovering signals, organizing opportunities, scoring what deserves attention, and connecting the strongest evidence to action.</p>
        <p>The public website is the first layer. A private operator system remains a future possibility only if real operational volume makes it necessary.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="loop" aria-label="Haidar System operating loop">
      <span>Think</span><span>Research</span><span>Build</span><span>Document</span><span>Publish</span><span>Learn</span>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
